Technical Assistance. The Department of Trade and Industry
shall assist the Autonomous Regional Government in facilitating the
performance of the latter's economic development mandate. The following
DII national bureaus may be tapped to provide support and technical
assistance to the Autonomous Regional Government:
].
Bureau of Export Trade Promotion (BETP):
Bureau of International Trade Relations (BITR);
Center for Labor Relations Assistance (CLARA);
Bureau of Import Servives (BIS);
Trade and Industry Information Center (TIC);
Bureau of Trade Regulation and Consumer Protection (BTRCP);
Bureau of Small and Medium Business Development (BSMBD);
Bureau of Patents, Trademarks and Technology Transfer (BPTTT);
Foreign Trade Service Corps (FTSC);
Bureau of Domestic Trade Promotion (BDTP); and
Bureau of Product Standards (BPS).
However, in view of its national implications, the powers and
functions of the Bureau of Export Trade Promotion (BETP) and the Bureau of
International Trade Relations (BIIR) shall be retained by the Department of
Trade and Industry without prejudice to whatever bureau or office the
Autonomous Regional Government shall create to coordinate with these
Bureaus. The Department of Trade and Industry may create a special action
team/group to ensure that the coordination on areas not allowed by law to be
devolved be coordinated to the fullest extent possible.
The Autonomous Regional Government may establish the appropriate
organizational unit that will allow it to implement the functions devolved by
the Department of Trade and Industry.
